{#
  Ukrainian fiscal receipt — the body SHARED by every UA fiscal-receipt archetype.

  A FRAGMENT, NOT AN ARCHETYPE, and the extension says so: `templates/*.html` is one
  renderable document each, and this file is included by three of them —
  `ua_prro_receipt` (80 mm ПРРО), `ua_prro_receipt_58mm` (58 mm ПРРО) and `ua_rro_receipt`
  (80 mm classic hardware РРО). It carries no `<slug>.css` of its own; each including
  template brings its own stylesheet, which is where the paper width lives.

  WHY ONE BODY FOR THREE ARCHETYPES, stated because the alternative looks like more work
  done rather than less. The three differ in the paper width and in the fiscal identity the
  register prints, and the second of those is DATA — which prefix the fiscal number carries,
  whether a «ЗН» line exists, whether the online marker appears, which maker's name is
  printed — all of it decided in `content_builder.build_prro_receipt` from
  `receipt.registrars` in config/fiscal-rules.yaml. Nothing about the LAYOUT differs.

  AND THAT IS A LIMIT WORTH NAMING RATHER THAN A CLAIM OF ELEGANCE. Real registers differ in
  layout by provider, and this body does not: ⛔ no open sample shows the layout of a
  hardware РРО beyond two published drawings, so a layout difference invented here would be a
  guess printed on every image of that archetype. What varies is what is evidenced; what is
  not evidenced is left identical, and the corpus therefore shows less layout diversity than
  three archetypes suggest.

  Layout follows the UA block of config/fiscal-rules.yaml. Two details of it are evidenced
  rather than guessed, and they have DIFFERENT sources:

    * the time is printed with dashes (14-22-51) and not colons — that is in
      `verified_against_own_receipts`;
    * the fiscal title sits near the FOOT of the receipt rather than at the head, which is
      evidenced publicly instead: the published form makes the wording its LAST line, and
      every open sample carries it at the bottom. The sequence WITHIN the foot block is a
      separate question and a weaker one — see the comment on that block below.

  Every element a consumer would extract carries data-field="<name>". The renderer reads
  getBoundingClientRect() for each of them in the same pass as the screenshot, so the
  boxes come from the browser's layout engine and are exact by construction. Repeated
  elements are indexed — item_0_name, item_1_name — because field_bboxes is a flat map.
#}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="uk">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<style>
{% for face in font_faces -%}
@font-face {
  font-family: "{{ face.family }}";
  src: url("{{ face.url }}") format("truetype");
  font-weight: 100 900;
  font-style: normal;
}
{% endfor -%}
{# The rules every UA fiscal receipt shares, then the including archetype's own stylesheet,
   which the renderer read from `<slug>.css` and which carries the paper width. In this order
   so that a per-archetype rule overrides the shared one rather than being overridden by it. #}
{% include "ua_fiscal_receipt.css" %}
{{ stylesheet | safe }}
</style>
</head>
<body>
{# data-document marks the page root. The renderer sizes the viewport to this element,
   so the image is the document and not the browser window around it. Every template
   carries exactly one — including through an include, which is how the three archetypes
   sharing this body satisfy that rule. #}
<div class="receipt" data-document="fiscal_receipt">

  <header class="block centered">
    <div class="seller-name" data-field="seller_name">{{ seller_display }}</div>
    <div data-field="seller_address">{{ seller.address }}</div>
    {# UP TO TWO identifier lines, each printed when the seller has that requisite — they are
       not alternatives, and a registered payer carries one MORE line than a non-payer rather
       than a different one. Every prefix comes from `identifiers` in config/fiscal-rules.yaml;
       a template cannot know what this seller holds, and a prefix written in here is what once
       put «ПН» on every sole trader's receipt.

       ORDER: ПН then ІД. 👁 Observed on the one receipt that carries both lines (1/1), and it
       agrees with 📄 the published table of the form, which numbers the VAT-payer number line 4
       and the identification code line 5. Two independent sources, one of them a real document,
       so the order is evidenced rather than inferred.

       «ІД» is printed on every document although 👁 only 1 of 3 real receipts carries one — the
       superset choice, and the overstatement it causes is declared under `known_limitations` in
       config/labelling-schema.yaml. The axis is the ПРРО software PROVIDER, not the seller, so
       the no-ІД variant is a further template rather than a flag, and none of the three
       registered today is it. #}
    {% if seller.vat_number %}
    <div>{{ seller.vat_number_label }} <span data-field="seller_vat_number">{{ seller.vat_number }}</span></div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if seller.tax_code %}
    <div>{{ seller.tax_code_label }} <span data-field="seller_tax_code">{{ seller.tax_code }}</span></div>
    {% endif %}
  </header>

  <div class="rule"></div>

  <section class="block">
    {% for item in items %}
    <div class="item">
      <div class="item-name" data-field="item_{{ loop.index0 }}_name">{{ item.name }}</div>
      <div class="row">
        <span class="item-qty">
          <span data-field="item_{{ loop.index0 }}_qty">{{ item.qty }}</span>
          &times;
          <span data-field="item_{{ loop.index0 }}_price">{{ item.price }}</span>
        </span>
        <span class="item-sum">
          <span data-field="item_{{ loop.index0 }}_sum">{{ item.sum }}</span>
          {# Omitted entirely, not left blank, when the seller is not registered for ПДВ: the
             observed line ends with the amount. An empty element would print a gap and leave
             a box pointing at nothing. #}
          {% if item.vat_letter %}
          <span class="vat-letter" data-field="item_{{ loop.index0 }}_vat_letter">{{ item.vat_letter }}</span>
          {% endif %}
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </section>

  <div class="rule"></div>

  {# FOUR lines, not one. СУМА and ДО СПЛАТИ are separate requisites of the form (lines 20 and
     24) and differ by the two between them; a merged "СУМА ДО СПЛАТИ" is neither of them. All
     four are printed even while the middle two are zero, because that is what the observed
     receipt does. Every label comes from `receipt.totals_labels` in config/fiscal-rules.yaml,
     which is also where the ЗАОКРУГЛЕННЯ (👁) against ОКРУГЛЕННЯ (📄) divergence is recorded.

     ORDER, AND WHAT IS NOT KNOWN ABOUT IT. The form numbers СУМА, then the tax rows, then the
     rounding, then ДО СПЛАТИ, and that is the order here. Where ЗНИЖКА sits RELATIVE TO THE
     TAX ROWS is not something any open sample shows: the one receipt observed to print
     ЗНИЖКА was issued by a seller with no VAT block, so the two never appeared together.
     Placing it immediately before ЗАОКРУГЛЕННЯ gives the same ORDER of these four lines as
     that receipt — a claim about their sequence only, not about the rest of the render — and
     follows the form's own numbering everywhere the form numbers a line. A seller that is not
     registered for ПДВ has no tax rows here at all. #}
  <section class="block">
    <div class="row total">
      <span>{{ totals_labels.total }}</span>
      <span data-field="total">{{ total }}</span>
    </div>
    {# The row itself carries the box, as the acquiring block's `operation` row does, so that
       one key still covers the whole requisite — the letter, the rate and the amount — while
       the amount sits in the receipt's amount column instead of hard against the label. #}
    {% for line in tax_lines %}
    <div class="row" data-field="tax_line_{{ loop.index0 }}">
      <span>{{ line.label }}</span>
      <span>{{ line.amount }}</span>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
    <div class="row">
      <span>{{ totals_labels.discount }}</span>
      <span data-field="discount">{{ discount }}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <span>{{ totals_labels.rounding }}</span>
      <span data-field="rounding">{{ rounding }}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="row total">
      <span>{{ totals_labels.amount_due }}</span>
      <span data-field="amount_due">{{ amount_due }}</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="rule"></div>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="row">
      <span data-field="payment_method">{{ payment_method }}</span>
      {# 🔴 «ДО СПЛАТИ» AND NOT «СУМА»: what is tendered is what is payable, which is the basket less
         the discount plus the cash rounding. This line read `total` until the pixel gate went in,
         and the two are equal on every document this generator builds only because `discount` and
         `rounding` are fixed at zero — so the corpus never showed the difference and no test could:
         the day a discount becomes a draw, a receipt printing `total` here would state a payment
         that does not settle its own «ДО СПЛАТИ» line, and the товарний чек beside it (which reads
         `amount_due`) would state a different one from the same basket. Fixed while it costs
         nothing rather than after a corpus carries it. #}
      <span data-field="paid_amount">{{ amount_due }}</span>
    </div>
    {% if acquiring %}
    <div>{{ acquiring_labels.acquirer }} <span data-field="acquirer">{{ acquiring.acquirer }}</span></div>
    <div>{{ acquiring_labels.terminal_id }} <span data-field="terminal_id">{{ acquiring.terminal_id }}</span></div>
    <div data-field="operation">{{ acquiring.operation }}</div>
    <div>{{ acquiring_labels.card_masked }} <span data-field="card_masked">{{ acquiring.card_masked }}</span></div>
    <div>{{ acquiring_labels.auth_code }} <span data-field="auth_code">{{ acquiring.auth_code }}</span></div>
    <div>{{ acquiring_labels.rrn }} <span data-field="rrn">{{ acquiring.rrn }}</span></div>
    {% endif %}
  </section>

  <div class="rule"></div>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="caption">Сума прописом:</div>
    <div data-field="amount_in_words">{{ amount_in_words }}</div>
  </section>

  <div class="rule"></div>

  {# The fiscal identity of the document. On a Ukrainian receipt this block sits at the foot.
     Three decisions here are contested by the sources, and each is settled the same way — by
     the authority that covers the document being built, with the losing evidence named.

     1. «ФІСКАЛЬНИЙ ЧЕК» IS PRINTED ON A NON-PAYER'S RECEIPT TOO, and that is a choice.
        📄 The Положення makes the wording line 35 of the form with no exemption for anyone,
        and 👁 8/8 open receipts of companies carry it. Against that, 👁 the single open
        photograph of a sole trader's receipt does NOT carry the wording at all — but that
        photograph is of the form in force BEFORE 01.03.2025, and ⛔ no post-change sole
        trader's receipt has been seen, so it cannot say what today's form does. One
        pre-change photograph does not outweigh a current norm plus eight current documents,
        so the norm wins. Stated because this is the most expensive field on the receipt to
        get wrong: it is what a classifier reads to decide the document is fiscal at all, and
        an error would sit on every image of the class.
     2. THE MAKER'S NAME SITS IMMEDIATELY AFTER THE WORDING, and this is the best-evidenced
        fact of the block: 📄 line 35 of the form is ONE requisite — the wording together with
        the name or logo of the виробник — and 👁 11 of 11 open receipts print such a name
        directly after it. The name comes from `receipt.registrars.<kind>.providers` in
        config/fiscal-rules.yaml, drawn with the title suffix beside it so the two cannot name
        different providers; it is never written into this markup, which could not know which
        register produced the document.
     3. THE SEQUENCE WITHIN THIS BLOCK is ЗН → ФН → title → maker → mode marker → QR → footer
        text, while 📄 the form's table numbers them QR 29, mode 31, ЗН 33, ФН 34 and the title
        35, last. So the sequence does not follow the form's numbering, and NOTHING IN THIS
        REPOSITORY RECORDS WHERE IT CAME FROM: every entry of `verified_against_own_receipts`
        in config/fiscal-rules.yaml is a fact about a value, a format or a field set, and none
        is an ordering — so a claim that the sequence is grounded there would be false.
        (Stated as a property of the list rather than as a count of it: the list grows, and a
        number written here would go stale without becoming visibly wrong.)

        Left as it is all the same, which is a decision rather than an oversight. ⛔ No open
        sample shows where the QR sits relative to the fiscal block, so any reordering would
        replace an unattributed arrangement with a guess, and the two load-bearing facts — the
        title near the foot, the maker's name immediately after it — are separately evidenced
        and already satisfied. Within the pair that IS numbered, ЗН precedes ФН as the form
        numbers them.

     WHICH LINES EXIST HERE FOLLOWS THE KIND OF REGISTER, and ⚠️ «ЗН» and «ФН» are not a pair:
     👁 a ПРРО prints the fiscal number alone and has no factory serial, 👁 the two published
     hardware samples print both. The online/offline marker is 📄 a ПРРО requisite (line 31),
     so a hardware receipt carries none. All of it arrives as data — `device_serial` and
     `mode_marker` are `None` where the line does not exist — so nothing here decides it. #}
  <footer class="block centered">
    <div>ЧЕК № <span data-field="receipt_number">{{ receipt_number }}</span></div>
    <div>
      <span data-field="date">{{ date }}</span>
      <span data-field="time">{{ time }}</span>
    </div>
    {% if device_serial %}
    <div>{{ device_serial_label }} <span data-field="device_serial">{{ device_serial }}</span></div>
    {% endif %}
    <div>{{ fiscal_number_label }} <span data-field="fiscal_device_number">{{ fiscal_device_number }}</span></div>
    <div class="fiscal-title" data-field="title">{{ title }}</div>
    <div data-field="provider_name">{{ provider_name }}</div>
    {% if mode_marker %}
    <div data-field="mode_marker">{{ mode_marker }}</div>
    {% endif %}
    <div class="qr" data-field="qr">{{ qr_svg | safe }}</div>
    <div class="thanks" data-field="footer_text">{{ footer }}</div>
  </footer>

</div>
</body>
</html>
